WEBVTT

00:00:08.134 --> 00:00:12.430
Look at the fluttering white
train on that jellyfish, honey.

00:00:12.513 --> 00:00:16.517
It's like the snow-white lace
on a princess's dress, isn't it?

00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:29.447
Tsukimi, when you get married
I'll make you a dress just like this, okay?

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:33.242
<i>--The jellyfish aquarium my morn took me to visit</i> when <i>I
was little...</i> --A <i>fluttery dress just like</i> a <i>princess's.</i>

00:00:33.242 --> 00:00:36.746
<i>“The jellyfish aquarium my morn took me to visit
when I was little...</i> --A <i>princess's dress...</i>

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:38.623
--Or is it weird that jellyfish
remind me of princesses?

00:00:38.623 --> 00:00:42.251
<i>--When she saw the fluttering frills on the jellyfish that looked like</i> a
<i>princess's dress, --Or is it weird that jellyfish remind me of princesses?</i>

00:00:42.335 --> 00:00:48.633
--she said: --Mm-mm! I want a
dress like these jellyfish!

00:00:48.716 --> 00:00:49.634
"They're so pretty!

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:58.768
<i>--"All girls can be beautiful princesses
when they grow up. “</i> --They're <i>so pretty!</i>

00:01:03.731 --> 00:01:05.900
What's that? Shibuya, you say?

00:01:07.276 --> 00:01:09.654
Have you gone mad? Shibuya, on a weekend?!

00:01:09.779 --> 00:01:11.447
"No Smoking While You Walk"

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:13.783
You would go there alone?

00:01:15.451 --> 00:01:18.412
How horrifying! Once, when I went there...

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.418
You still insist on going?!

00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:29.006
"Nun"

00:01:29.548 --> 00:01:33.761
Please keep what I'm about to sing

00:01:35.221 --> 00:01:37.223
<i>Just between us, okay?</i>

00:01:37.306 --> 00:01:43.020
<i>The truth is, I want to keep my
desires hidden deep in my heart</i>

00:01:43.104 --> 00:01:45.147
<i>A secret, a secret</i>

00:02:01.414 --> 00:02:04.000
<i>I</i> want <i>to take shortcuts</i>

00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:07.878
<i>Never getting soaked by the rain</i>

00:02:07.962 --> 00:02:11.507
<i>Never getting knocked over by the wind</i>

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:15.303
<i>Even if that's being devious, smile</i>

00:02:15.386 --> 00:02:19.765
<i>Even if I'm a coward, play with me</i>

00:02:20.766 --> 00:02:23.352
<i>I don't</i> want <i>to feel sad</i>

00:02:23.436 --> 00:02:27.189
<i>Never getting soaked by tears</i>

00:02:27.273 --> 00:02:30.818
<i>Never feeling at my wit's end</i>

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:34.322
<i>Just smile and think I'm insensitive</i>

00:02:34.405 --> 00:02:39.368
<i>Only tell me about fun things</i>

00:02:43.122 --> 00:02:47.668
<i>See, there are faces I</i> want <i>to
see and voices I</i> want <i>to hear</i>

00:02:48.878 --> 00:02:52.548
<i>When I wake up I trumpet my joy:</i>

00:02:52.631 --> 00:02:58.596
Good morning!
Let's have another fine day!

00:02:58.596 --> 00:02:58.888
"Princess Jellyfish"

00:03:02.016 --> 00:03:07.104
Mom... Mom, you were right.

00:03:07.188 --> 00:03:09.690
<i>It's already been six
months since I left for Tokyo</i>

00:03:09.774 --> 00:03:12.234
<i>to try to make it as an illustrator.</i>

00:03:12.318 --> 00:03:18.324
<i>Here in the metropolis of Tokyo,
there are</i> a <i>lot of princesses.</i>

00:03:18.407 --> 00:03:25.873
But I'm sorry, Mom... <i>I</i> have some bad news.

00:03:25.956 --> 00:03:30.920
<i>I'm not sure where I went wrong,
but somewhere along the line,</i>

00:03:31.003 --> 00:03:34.173
instead of becoming a princess...

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.139
I-I'm going home...

00:03:42.223 --> 00:03:44.892
Yeah. I'll just go home.

00:03:44.975 --> 00:03:47.937
...I <i>ended</i> up a freak.

00:03:49.355 --> 00:03:52.316
"Sex and the Sisterhood"

00:03:52.483 --> 00:03:55.069
Tsukimi has returned to us!

00:03:56.362 --> 00:03:58.447
Tsukimi Kurashita, age eighteen,

00:03:58.531 --> 00:04:01.283
has returned from Shibuya alive and well!

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.035
Tsukimi!

00:04:03.119 --> 00:04:05.079
Thank goodness you're safe!

00:04:12.169 --> 00:04:17.508
And so, before I made it to the photo
exhibition at this "Parco" place,

00:04:17.591 --> 00:04:21.095
I was assailed by dizziness, heart
palpitations, and shortness of breath,

00:04:21.178 --> 00:04:23.097
forcing me into a tearful retreat.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.849
Hey, me too--

00:04:24.932 --> 00:04:26.851
So even your great jellyfish love

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:29.395
couldn't propel you into that Pandemonium!

00:04:29.478 --> 00:04:33.023
I'm dismayed. I should have gone on a weekday.

00:04:33.107 --> 00:04:35.484
The crowd at the station was especially huge...

00:04:35.568 --> 00:04:37.361
Th-That's right. I too--

00:04:37.445 --> 00:04:39.363
Shibuya's always been a traffic hub.

00:04:39.447 --> 00:04:41.949
The old Tamagawa streetcars
and whatnot all flourished there.

00:04:42.032 --> 00:04:43.200
Wow.

00:04:44.034 --> 00:04:46.996
They once carried me to the station
office when I swooned from anemia...

00:04:47.079 --> 00:04:50.249
I don't know whether I should give
it another shot tomorrow or not...

00:04:50.332 --> 00:04:53.043
You reckless lover of adventure!

00:04:53.127 --> 00:04:54.753
Don't do it, Tsukimi.

00:04:54.879 --> 00:04:57.590
--There's no way you could make it back alive. --Mom,
<i>I</i> couldn't manage to become a beautiful princess,

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:02.720
--Mom, <i>I</i> couldn't manage
to <i>become</i> a beautiful princess,

00:05:02.803 --> 00:05:05.973
<i>but I have a really fun life here in Tokyo.</i>

00:05:07.266 --> 00:05:10.978
I did manage to get the
things you all requested...

00:05:11.061 --> 00:05:12.438
Oh, object of my desire!

00:05:12.521 --> 00:05:16.734
This is what you were
asking about, right Banba?

00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:21.280
<i>I've been living in this
communal apartment building</i>

00:05:21.363 --> 00:05:23.324
<i>--since some friends I met in an online
community invited me three months ago.</i>

00:05:23.324 --> 00:05:25.993
<i>--You didn't ask me for anything, Chieko, "since some friends
I met in an online community invited me</i> three <i>months</i> ago.

00:05:26.076 --> 00:05:27.786
But on my way home I saw this...

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:31.290
<i>All the residents are kind
and considerate people,</i>

00:05:31.373 --> 00:05:35.377
<i>and I'm happy to say that they're all like</i> me...

00:05:35.461 --> 00:05:39.465
Oh, and for you, Mayaya, here's
something from Akihabara Station.

00:05:40.549 --> 00:05:43.385
Akihabara-version Three Kingdoms figurines!

00:05:43.469 --> 00:05:44.512
I didn't look inside.

00:05:44.595 --> 00:05:47.181
<i>They're all freaks.</i>

00:05:47.264 --> 00:05:49.183
Xiahou Dun!

00:05:49.266 --> 00:05:51.310
Xiahou Yuan!

00:05:51.393 --> 00:05:53.020
Cao Cao!

00:05:53.103 --> 00:05:55.523
A truly godly grouping!

00:05:55.606 --> 00:05:57.149
“The Kingdom of Wei
has come to the Nunnery!

00:05:57.149 --> 00:05:58.442
--Um, what about me...? --The Kingdom
of VVei has come to the Nunnery!

00:05:58.442 --> 00:05:59.777
<i>“Um, what about me...'? --They've each got different
interests, but they're a“ otaku to the core.</i>

00:05:59.777 --> 00:06:04.198
--Oh, <i>the flyer? Yes,</i> I <i>got it. --They've each got
different interests, but they're all otaku to the core.</i>

00:06:04.198 --> 00:06:05.032
<i>--They've each got different interests,
but they're all otaku to the core.</i>

00:06:05.115 --> 00:06:09.995
--I'm so sorry! It got crinkled while the crowd was
pushing at me... --And naturally they have no boyfriends.

00:06:11.664 --> 00:06:16.252
So <i>we</i> call ourselves...

00:06:16.961 --> 00:06:19.922
...The Sisterhood.

00:06:19.922 --> 00:06:21.131
"The Sisterhood"

00:06:23.259 --> 00:06:24.593
Oh, we have another email

00:06:24.677 --> 00:06:26.595
from someone wanting to
live here at Amamizu-kan.

00:06:26.679 --> 00:06:29.431
I wish this would stop.
Yes, we have an empty room,

00:06:29.515 --> 00:06:32.226
but we don't take people we don't
know with no one to vouch for them!

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:34.103
There've been a lot of these requests lately

00:06:34.186 --> 00:06:36.855
from people in the Sisterhood
community, haven't there?

00:06:36.939 --> 00:06:40.859
Yes. And it's such a bother to
refuse each one individually...

00:06:40.943 --> 00:06:43.904
Maybe it's time we decided
on some rules for applicants.

00:06:43.988 --> 00:06:47.866
Times like this call for one thing:
a consult with Ms. Mejiro!

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:52.329
Good idea. Write her a note,
would you, Mayaya?

00:06:53.163 --> 00:06:54.123
At once!

00:06:54.915 --> 00:06:58.210
"More and more people are asking to live here.

00:06:58.294 --> 00:07:00.963
We'd like to post clear and
simple application requirements

00:07:01.046 --> 00:07:03.924
on the community home page, but..."

00:07:04.008 --> 00:07:06.176
Yes, I think this is fine.

00:07:08.178 --> 00:07:11.140
Most honored Ms. Mejiro!

00:07:11.223 --> 00:07:14.393
We humbly request your decree!

00:07:22.109 --> 00:07:24.945
A motorcycle courier came
by here this morning, right?

00:07:25.029 --> 00:07:29.783
Yes. She's just made a deadline,
so she should be taking it easy today.

00:07:29.867 --> 00:07:32.620
Do you think she'll come out?

00:07:32.703 --> 00:07:36.415
She's anthropophobic and nocturnal,
and she's a best-selling manga artist

00:07:36.498 --> 00:07:39.752
who was once called
"the Grand Dame of Boys' Love,"

00:07:39.835 --> 00:07:43.213
so her days off are devoted to sleep.

00:07:43.297 --> 00:07:46.467
It's just that I'd like to see her sometime...

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.385
lriomote Wildcats.

00:07:48.469 --> 00:07:49.386
Pardon?

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:51.388
Sighting her is as rare as sighting them.

00:07:51.472 --> 00:07:55.309
My mother put me in charge of
managing this building five years ago,

00:07:55.392 --> 00:07:59.355
and even I've only seen her a handful of times.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:03.067
Here it comes!

00:08:06.904 --> 00:08:08.739
"A Life that Has No Use for Men"

00:08:08.947 --> 00:08:10.324
That's our Ms. Mejiro!

00:08:10.407 --> 00:08:13.786
<i>The last time I went out
somewhere with my</i> mom...

00:08:15.162 --> 00:08:19.875
<i>...it was a solitary little
jellyfish aquarium by the sea</i>

00:08:19.958 --> 00:08:22.920
<i>in my hometown of Kagoshima.</i>

00:08:26.882 --> 00:08:32.554
<i>The snow-white jellyfish I saw
with her were so very beautiful</i>

00:08:32.638 --> 00:08:36.600
<i>that I was thoroughly bewitched by them.</i>

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:42.690
Look! This is a flower hat jelly!
It's really colorful, right?

00:08:42.773 --> 00:08:44.566
And this one's a spotted jelly.

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:48.654
The book says it's called that
cuz it looks like a spotted octopus!

00:08:48.737 --> 00:08:51.782
Sounds like you're a real expert now, Tsukimi.

00:08:51.865 --> 00:08:54.660
Well, yeah! Check this out, Mom!

00:08:54.743 --> 00:08:58.288
When you write "jellyfish" in kanji,
it's spelled "sea moon."

00:08:58.372 --> 00:09:01.834
And if you flip that to
"moon sea," it spells "Tsukimi"!

00:09:01.917 --> 00:09:06.922
Didja name me after a jellyfish, Mom?

00:09:07.005 --> 00:09:10.384
Come on, even I wouldn't
name you after a jellyfish!

00:09:10.467 --> 00:09:13.679
I've told you a hundred times,
I named you "Tsukimi"

00:09:13.762 --> 00:09:18.392
because you were born by the sea on
a night when the moon was so pretty.

00:09:18.475 --> 00:09:20.269
Whoops, I forgot!

00:09:28.026 --> 00:09:34.825
<i>When I get lonely remembering
Mom, I always go visit Clara.</i>

00:09:37.494 --> 00:09:40.789
Clara! I haven't seen you in two days!

00:09:40.873 --> 00:09:42.875
How've you been?

00:09:42.958 --> 00:09:48.464
You've really got it good.
I wish I could float with you.

00:09:48.547 --> 00:09:51.633
Oh, hey, you've got a new fri-

00:09:51.717 --> 00:09:55.846
Is that... a moon jelly?

00:09:55.929 --> 00:09:58.056
No! This is wrong!

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:01.977
I read that if you put a spotted jelly
and a moon jelly in the same tank,

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.354
the spotted jelly will weaken and die!

00:10:04.438 --> 00:10:07.608
The shopkeeper must not know!
I have to tell him!

00:10:10.319 --> 00:10:11.695
<i>That's...!</i>

00:10:12.905 --> 00:10:16.867
<i>I-It's one of the Stylish! And a boy!</i>

00:10:16.867 --> 00:10:17.326
"Stylish Ring"

00:10:27.002 --> 00:10:28.212
<i>It's impossible!</i>

00:10:28.295 --> 00:10:32.633
<i>I couldn't start</i> a <i>conversation with</i> a
<i>male Stylish if my life depended on it!</i>

00:10:32.716 --> 00:10:33.675
But...

00:10:35.761 --> 00:10:38.764
Tsukimi, help me!

00:10:38.847 --> 00:10:40.182
Clara!

00:10:40.265 --> 00:10:43.602
Please help me, Tsukimi!

00:10:43.685 --> 00:10:44.728
Clara!

00:10:44.812 --> 00:10:47.981
I'm in serious pain here!

00:10:48.065 --> 00:10:50.734
Clara!

00:10:50.818 --> 00:10:52.361
Tsukimi!

00:10:52.444 --> 00:10:54.279
Clara!

00:10:54.363 --> 00:10:55.489
Tsukimi!

00:10:55.572 --> 00:10:58.116
Clara!

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.453
She stood up! She stood up! Clara stood up!

00:11:01.537 --> 00:11:03.497
Clara stood up!

00:11:15.884 --> 00:11:19.805
Look, what do you want?
We're closed right now.

00:11:19.888 --> 00:11:22.975
Um, o-o-over there, th-th-that...

00:11:23.058 --> 00:11:23.475
<i>Yes'?</i>

00:11:23.517 --> 00:11:26.395
I-In that aquarium's sp-spotted jelly,

00:11:26.478 --> 00:11:28.814
th-there's a moon jelly!

00:11:28.897 --> 00:11:31.733
Huh?

00:11:31.817 --> 00:11:36.655
I'm sure you know how incredibly
difficult it is to raise jellyfish.

00:11:36.738 --> 00:11:39.449
It's generally accepted that
if you raise a spotted jelly

00:11:39.533 --> 00:11:41.869
and a moon jelly together in such a small tank,

00:11:41.952 --> 00:11:44.913
the spotted jelly, a member
of the Rhizostomeae order,

00:11:44.997 --> 00:11:47.583
will be weakened by the
moon jelly's mucus and die.

00:11:47.666 --> 00:11:49.001
--Honestly, why would
even you put them together

00:11:49.001 --> 00:11:50.210
--Sorry, but the boss is out right now, so could you come back
tomorrow? --Honestly, why would even you put them together

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:54.506
--Sorry, but the boss is out right now, so could you come back
tomorrow? --when you have so many tanks here in the first place--?!

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:56.633
Tomorrow... will be... too... late!

00:11:56.717 --> 00:11:59.970
Hey! Stop it! I'll call the police!

00:12:00.053 --> 00:12:02.431
--Hurry up and--
--Let go.

00:12:02.514 --> 00:12:04.892
Let go! I said let me go!

00:12:04.975 --> 00:12:07.144
You freakin' otaku chick!

00:12:11.148 --> 00:12:13.317
Whoa, are you okay?

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:16.361
E-Excuse me! I...

00:12:17.279 --> 00:12:22.075
<i>Mom, the person standing there...</i>

00:12:23.827 --> 00:12:26.204
...was a princess.

00:12:27.623 --> 00:12:28.582
It's commercial time!

00:12:28.665 --> 00:12:30.000
Clara!

00:12:30.959 --> 00:12:32.127
It's the second half!

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:33.003
Tequila!

00:12:37.925 --> 00:12:39.635
Lovers' quarrel?

00:12:39.718 --> 00:12:43.263
N-No! Why would I go out with a girl like that?!

00:12:43.347 --> 00:12:45.182
I don't know her.

00:12:45.265 --> 00:12:49.561
What, then you knocked
over some girl you don't know?

00:12:49.645 --> 00:12:53.982
W-Well, she was talking crazy
and she tried to come in here, so...

00:12:54.066 --> 00:12:56.193
N-No!

00:12:56.276 --> 00:13:00.155
I just wanted him to transfer
that jellyfish to another tank!

00:13:00.238 --> 00:13:02.157
Because if he doesn't, it'll die soon!

00:13:03.408 --> 00:13:05.369
Yes, it'll die!

00:13:06.703 --> 00:13:10.040
Then why don't you take it?

00:13:10.123 --> 00:13:14.086
That's no problem, right? Give us that jellyfish.

00:13:18.131 --> 00:13:19.424
But my boss...

00:13:19.508 --> 00:13:24.763
Tell him it died! If you don't do
something, it'll be dead anyway.

00:13:24.846 --> 00:13:29.434
It <i>will</i> die before long, right?
This thing. The jellyfish.

00:13:30.769 --> 00:13:33.230
Y-Yes! It'll die!

00:13:33.313 --> 00:13:36.108
It's already dead, if you like!

00:13:39.152 --> 00:13:41.905
Jellyfish are pretty troublesome, aren't they?

00:13:41.989 --> 00:13:44.616
I thought all you had to do
was stick 'em in some water.

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:49.204
L-I'm sorry, I'll pay you
back as soon as I get home.

00:13:49.287 --> 00:13:52.249
Nah, don't worry about it. This was fun!

00:13:52.332 --> 00:13:54.126
<i>“Fun“ ...'?</i>

00:14:06.054 --> 00:14:06.888
Which way?

00:14:06.972 --> 00:14:09.808
Huh? Oh!

00:14:09.891 --> 00:14:11.268
This way.

00:14:13.186 --> 00:14:15.022
We will soon be arriving in Shibuya.

00:14:15.105 --> 00:14:17.274
Change here for the Tokyu
Toyoko Line, the Den-en-toshi Line,

00:14:17.357 --> 00:14:21.945
the Keio Inokashira Line, the Ginza
Subway Line, and the Hanzomon Line.

00:14:34.374 --> 00:14:38.962
Yes, you've got such a nice figure,
it looks perfect on you, Midoriko!

00:14:41.048 --> 00:14:46.595
The essence of my parents
cannot be thrown away!

00:14:46.678 --> 00:14:49.264
Curse you, Cao Xing!

00:14:52.225 --> 00:14:55.937
"No Boys Allowed "

00:14:55.937 --> 00:14:57.272
Wow, this is a neat building!

00:14:57.355 --> 00:14:59.483
Shh! Please, be quiet!

00:14:59.566 --> 00:15:01.276
What, do you have a curfew or something?

00:15:01.359 --> 00:15:05.280
N-No, but it could be bad if the
others saw someone like you here...

00:15:05.363 --> 00:15:06.156
Huh?!

00:15:06.198 --> 00:15:09.242
No, no, I didn't mean it like that.

00:15:09.326 --> 00:15:13.038
You could say we're from different races,
or maybe from different worlds...

00:15:13.121 --> 00:15:16.500
Huh, I guess you can tell, then.

00:15:16.833 --> 00:15:19.628
"Sea Salt Mix"

00:15:19.628 --> 00:15:23.131
Sorry, Clara. I'll go buy an aquarium
first thing in the morning, okay?

00:15:23.215 --> 00:15:25.133
Hey, she's swimming!

00:15:25.217 --> 00:15:27.010
Thank goodness.

00:15:28.678 --> 00:15:34.226
Um, thank you. You're Clara's savior.

00:15:34.309 --> 00:15:37.104
I think "savior" is a bit much.

00:15:38.522 --> 00:15:41.483
So, um, well...

00:15:41.566 --> 00:15:44.069
I'm very sorry to ask you this...

00:15:44.152 --> 00:15:47.531
...but would you mind leaving?

00:15:50.534 --> 00:15:52.452
Through the window, quick!

00:15:52.536 --> 00:15:55.872
The window? I can't do that.

00:15:55.956 --> 00:15:57.749
O-One of the Stylish!

00:15:59.292 --> 00:16:02.712
Oh, no! Mayaya's turned to stone!

00:16:02.796 --> 00:16:05.924
Pull yourself together, Mayaya!

00:16:06.007 --> 00:16:08.385
Who is that woman?!

00:16:10.428 --> 00:16:12.597
There's a jellyfish in the bath!

00:16:12.681 --> 00:16:15.642
--I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!
--You want me to bathe with a jellyfish?!

00:16:17.144 --> 00:16:20.605
Did you draw all these jellyfish pictures?

00:16:20.689 --> 00:16:25.861
Wow. What's this one that looks like beads?

00:16:25.944 --> 00:16:28.280
Er, that's a flower hat jelly.

00:16:28.363 --> 00:16:29.322
And this one?

00:16:29.406 --> 00:16:30.782
A comb jelly.

00:16:30.866 --> 00:16:32.242
So they're sparkly...

00:16:32.325 --> 00:16:35.203
Yes, strictly speaking,
comb jellies are actually ctenophores,

00:16:35.287 --> 00:16:38.248
not cnidarians like real jellyfish,

00:16:38.331 --> 00:16:40.917
and the cilia in those lines
on their bodies reflect light,

00:16:41.001 --> 00:16:43.253
shining like rainbows,
as exquisitely beautiful as--

00:16:43.336 --> 00:16:48.300
Oh, this one's gorgeous! It's kind of like lace.

00:16:48.383 --> 00:16:50.385
Snow-white lace.

00:16:53.972 --> 00:16:55.348
Can I use this?

00:16:55.432 --> 00:16:56.183
“What? No! Hey... Wait...

00:16:56.183 --> 00:16:59.436
--I stayed out partying all night again, and
I'm so wiped. --What? No! Hey... VVait...

00:16:59.436 --> 00:17:01.605
--Lemme take a quick nap, okay?
“What? No! Hey... Wait...

00:17:04.149 --> 00:17:05.108
She's asleep?!

00:17:16.703 --> 00:17:20.165
"Nun"

00:17:20.248 --> 00:17:23.418
Yes. I heard the butler Tokiwazaka
will be working today only

00:17:23.501 --> 00:17:25.462
at their sister bar in Shibuya...

00:17:25.545 --> 00:17:29.633
Tsukimi was slain in battle at Shibuya!
Do you go there for revenge?!

00:17:29.716 --> 00:17:32.594
Do you insist on going though
I, Guan Yu, tell you not to?!

00:17:32.677 --> 00:17:35.513
<i>L-I'll</i> be fine. Just for the occasion--

00:17:35.597 --> 00:17:36.806
Shibuya, eh?

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:40.936
Those power failures from the Ginza
Line's third rail really had atmosphere.

00:17:41.019 --> 00:17:42.103
Just for the occasion--

00:17:42.187 --> 00:17:43.355
Girls!

00:17:43.438 --> 00:17:45.607
What happened to the bathroom?

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:48.109
Just for the occasion...

00:17:48.193 --> 00:17:51.363
...I bought iron pills!

00:17:51.363 --> 00:17:52.572
"I'm very sorry. I'll be buying an aquarium tomorrow, so
please let her be for just a little while... -Tsukimi"

00:18:03.291 --> 00:18:07.671
Oh, right... She stayed overnight...

00:18:18.598 --> 00:18:22.310
<i>It's... a wig'?</i>

00:18:22.394 --> 00:18:24.854
Come to think of it, <i>I</i> remember reading

00:18:24.938 --> 00:18:28.108
<i>that the Stylish are into wigs
as fashion statements lately.</i>

00:18:41.663 --> 00:18:45.166
<i>Only the gods should be able
to make someone look this bad!</i>

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:51.423
<i>Mom, I never knew such beautiful people existed.</i>

00:18:51.923 --> 00:18:54.926
That's no problem, right? Give us that jellyfish.

00:18:55.010 --> 00:19:00.015
<i>Tall, fair-skinned, big-eyed...</i>

00:19:00.098 --> 00:19:03.852
<i>Just like</i> a <i>Barbie doll.</i>

00:19:03.935 --> 00:19:07.689
She's <i>living</i> boldly, using
that beauty as a weapon.

00:19:07.772 --> 00:19:11.067
<i>A girl the complete opposite of</i> me...

00:19:11.151 --> 00:19:13.945
<i>A girl who's just like a princess.</i>

00:19:18.408 --> 00:19:20.243
Isn't that wig great?

00:19:20.327 --> 00:19:22.704
S-Sorry! I don't know what came over me!

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:28.543
I got that thing on the internet for 13,000 yen.

00:19:30.628 --> 00:19:33.298
Huh? Sorry, didn't I tell you?

00:19:33.381 --> 00:19:35.383
A m-m-m-m-m-m--

00:19:35.467 --> 00:19:37.552
Tsukimi!

00:19:37.635 --> 00:19:41.056
--A m-m-m-m-m-m--

00:19:41.056 --> 00:19:43.433
--Why'd you push me?
--A m-m-m-m-m-m--

00:19:43.433 --> 00:19:45.769
"Yeah, I'm a man.
--A m-m-m-m-m-m--

00:19:45.852 --> 00:19:47.645
A-A-Are you a drag queen?

00:19:47.729 --> 00:19:51.733
What? No, cross-dressing's just my hobby.

00:19:51.816 --> 00:19:53.360
I'm normal.

00:19:53.443 --> 00:19:55.653
Wh-What about you is "normal"?!

00:19:55.737 --> 00:19:58.573
Anyway, would you lend
me some makeup remover?

00:19:58.656 --> 00:20:01.785
I fell asleep without washing
my face, and now it feels gross.

00:20:01.868 --> 00:20:05.330
<i>L-|-l</i> don't own anything like that!

00:20:05.413 --> 00:20:06.873
You're kidding. Why not?

00:20:06.956 --> 00:20:13.546
"Why not"? Er, I'm not particularly
in the habit of painting my face...

00:20:15.048 --> 00:20:16.508
You don't wear makeup?

00:20:16.591 --> 00:20:18.176
No, no, I don't!

00:20:18.259 --> 00:20:22.639
Oh, but they did put lipstick on me
for the Shichi-go-san Festival once!

00:20:22.722 --> 00:20:24.182
Wh-What?!

00:20:24.265 --> 00:20:27.060
Hey... are you a virgin?

00:20:32.732 --> 00:20:34.109
Clara here!

00:20:34.192 --> 00:20:36.277
Coming in at #1 on this week's

00:20:36.277 --> 00:20:38.279
"Top Five Things You
Shouldn't Ask the Sisterhood"

00:20:38.279 --> 00:20:38.738
Top Five Things You
Shouldn't Ask the Sisterhood:

00:20:38.738 --> 00:20:40.532
"Are you a virgin?"

00:20:40.532 --> 00:20:41.199
Are you a virgin?

00:20:42.242 --> 00:20:44.077
Vi-Vi--

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:47.080
I get it, so that's why
you're flipping out so much.

00:20:47.163 --> 00:20:49.582
Don't worry, I won't attack you.

00:20:51.209 --> 00:20:56.005
Oh, well. Guess I'll have to use soap.

00:20:56.089 --> 00:20:58.133
Please don't go out into the hallway!

00:20:58.216 --> 00:21:00.718
Why not? The sink's out there, isn't it?

00:21:00.802 --> 00:21:02.512
Th-The point is, you can't do it!

00:21:02.595 --> 00:21:04.305
If you're going out there, please,
please put on some clothes!

00:21:04.389 --> 00:21:07.183
And please put on your wig and dress in drag!

00:21:07.267 --> 00:21:09.936
Tsukimi, are you awake?

00:21:10.019 --> 00:21:13.690
<i>Mom, there's a princess here in Tokyo.</i>

00:21:13.773 --> 00:21:19.362
--Say, are you feeling all right?
--A strong, beautiful... MALE princess!

00:21:21.197 --> 00:21:30.206
<i>I really want you to
realize that you're gorgeous</i>

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:34.627
<i>Why haven't you realized it before this?</i>

00:21:34.711 --> 00:21:39.132
<i>It's like you've lost your heart</i>

00:21:39.215 --> 00:21:48.308
<i>I</i> want you to realize <i>it</i> right away,
right away, <i>I</i> want you to understand

00:21:48.391 --> 00:22:02.780
<i>I want you to realize it right</i> away,
<i>I want you to realize your beauty</i>

00:22:04.157 --> 00:22:08.620
<i>Because you're so very beautiful</i>

00:22:08.703 --> 00:22:12.707
<i>I want to convey that to you</i>

00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:22.383
<i>Your loveliness, forever and ever</i>

00:22:22.467 --> 00:22:30.808
<i>I'll be so happy if you'll
just realize your loveliness</i>

00:22:30.892 --> 00:22:35.605
<i>I</i> care about you, you know

00:22:35.688 --> 00:22:44.948
Please, realize your beauty
